Description: spiDE identifies context-specific, neighbourhood-dependent
    differential expression in spatial transcriptomics data. Within an index
    cell type, it asks whether a gene's expression changes with the local
    density (niche) of another cell type within patients, and whether that
    dependence differs between two conditions. Niche covariates are Gaussian
    kernel density estimates of each cell type. For every index cell type a
    per-gene negative binomial GLM with a patient intercept is fitted with
    SpaNorm's Newton solver; its niche slopes are then tested across patients,
    either from each patient's own slopes with weighted limma (the slopes
    engine) or with a patient-clustered CR2 sandwich (the sandwich engine).
    The pooled test asks whether a slope is consistently non-zero; the
    condition-specific test whether it differs between conditions.
